WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.182
Day-of-week values need documentation. In PostgreSQL, EXTRACT DOW uses zero for Sunday and six for Saturday.

00:00:08.182 --> 00:00:10.852
Other tools may use different conventions.

00:00:10.852 --> 00:00:19.782
Whenever a numeric code represents a temporal category, document the mapping before using it in analysis or

00:00:19.782 --> 00:00:26.812
modeling. Connect this idea to an operations team aligning timestamps across locations.

00:00:26.812 --> 00:00:31.427
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:31.427 --> 00:00:40.462
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:40.462 --> 00:00:46.457
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:46.457 --> 00:00:53.520
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
